# L §5.14.1 Running reads (round 12): "A span past the reader's day, in a binding or in flows, is its future, refused
# as a plain bal(x, d) after its day is (LOAD-CYCLE where load sees the day, RUN-FUTURE otherwise)": second, on the 5th,
# binds over sweeps through day_of(m, late), the 28th, known only at run: RUN-FUTURE. (Writer 5's T-65.)
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input amt: money PLN
input dom: int
input late: int
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place savings: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
kind sweeps: transfers

move first[m in months]: sweeps
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to savings amount min(amt, bal(konto))

version plan_2026
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 1 000.00 PLN "own"
  dom = 5 "own"
  late = 28 "own"
  opening[konto] = 5 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[savings] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

move second[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  after first
  reads first
  leg cash from konto to savings amount amt * count(x in sweeps over day_of(m, dom) .. day_of(m, late))

ask q: flows(second, 2026-01-01 .. 2026-01-31)
=== expect
q: refused: RUN-FUTURE ...
...
